  "full_response": "**Incident Report: Unauthorized External Sharing of INTERNAL_ONLY Documents**\n\n**Date of Incident:** [Insert Date]  \n**Incident Reported By:** [Name/Position]  \n**Reported By:** [Name/Position], [Department]  \n**Incident Number:** [Insert Unique Incident Number]\n\n**Background:**\nThe documents in question were classified under the \"INTERNAL_ONLY\" designation, indicating that access and distribution are strictly limited to personnel with the necessary clearance and justification. These documents contain sensitive information pertaining to [brief description of the content], which is critical to the operational security and integrity of our [organization/department/project].\n\n**Incident Description:**\nOn [Date/Time], [Employee's Name], [Employee's Position], inadvertently shared a file containing INTERNAL_ONLY documents via an unsecured email communication system to an external recipient. The file, identified as [Document File Name], was intended exclusively for internal review and use as per the company's information governance policy.\n\n**Analysis of Incident:**\nThe incident occurred during [brief description of activity where the error happened, e.g., \"routine document sharing for project review purposes\"], where [Employee's Name] mistakenly addressed the email to an external party. The recipient, who is not authorized to access INTERNAL_ONLY information, triggered an immediate alert upon receipt due to our email security protocols.\n\n**Immediate Actions Taken:**\n1. **Notification and Recall:** The information security team was notified, and they issued an immediate request to recall the email and delete any attachments. The recipient was instructed not to open the attachment.\n2. **Access Review:** [Employee's Name]'s access rights and recent activities were reviewed to ensure no further breaches have occurred.\n3. **Communication with Affected Parties:** Internal stakeholders were briefed on the incident to assess any potential impact and reinforce appropriate handling of INTERNAL_ONLY documents.\n4. **Incident Triage:** A thorough investigation was conducted to understand the scope of the disclosure and any possible repercussions.\n\n**Root Cause Analysis:**\nThe incident appears to be a result of human error rather than systemic failure. [Employee's Name] may have misjudged the intended recipient due to [possible factors, e.g., similar email domain, unfamiliarity with recipient, over-reliance on email auto-fill features].\n\n**Corrective and Preventative Measures:**\n1. **Re-Training:** A mandatory refresher training session on data classification and sharing procedures, specifically highlighting INTERNAL_ONLY documentation, has been scheduled for all relevant employees.\n2. **Enhanced Email Filtering:** Email systems will be",
